/*visual: A boundary diagram showing Terraform's responsibility in Kubernetes: Cluster creation, namespaces, RBAC, storage classes, operator installation (infrastructure tier) vs. Kubectl/Helm/ArgoCD's responsibility: Deployments, Services, Ingresses, ConfigMaps, HPAs (application tier). Clear vertical line separating the two tiers.*/
/*visual: A complete end-to-end pipeline flow: Developer pushes code -> GitHub Actions runs CI -> Docker builds image -> Trivy scans -> ECR push -> Kustomize patches image tag -> kubectl apply -> Kubernetes rolling deployment -> health check passes -> traffic routes to new pods*/
/*visual: A dependency graph showing the four tools with directed arrows representing explicit dependencies: VPC (Terraform) -> EKS Cluster (Terraform) -> Namespace/RBAC (Terraform/Kubernetes) -> External Secrets Operator (Helm/Terraform) -> Application Secrets (ExternalSecret CR) -> Application Deployment (Kubernetes/CI) <- Docker Image (Docker/CI)*/
const {Fragment: _Fragment, jsx: _jsx, jsxs: _jsxs} = arguments[0];
